      "id": "wait-at-place",
      "pattern": "[Verb] + فِي الـ[Place]",
      "exampleArabic": "أنتظر في المطعم",
      "exampleTransliteration": "antaẓiru fī l-maṭʿami",
      "exampleEnglish": "I wait at the restaurant.",
      "grammarNote": "اِنْتَظَرَ ('to wait') is Form VIII (اِفْتَعَلَ) — marked by an inserted تَـ after the first root letter: اِنْتَظَرَ, not اِنَظَرَ. Like Form V (level 62), Form VIII's present-tense prefix takes fatha, not damma: أَنْتَظِرُ, تَنْتَظِرُ, تَنْتَظِرِينَ, يَنْتَظِرُ, نَنْتَظِرُ. Five of the ten verb forms are now covered outside the base Form I: III (سافر), II (علّم), IV (أرسل), V (تعلم), and now VIII (انتظر).",
      "audio": { "id": "phrase_antaziru_fi_almatam", "text": "أنتظر في المطعم" },
      "introducedInLevel": 63
    }
  ],
